## PHASE 3 — DSR RIGHT-TO-FORGET / ERASURE

Implement a proper AG-002 data-subject erasure capability.

This is NOT merely soft-delete.

Requirements:

* Introduce an explicit erasure operation.
* Require appropriate authorization.
* Fail closed.
* Validate actor context.
* Support namespace/tenant ownership boundaries.
* Permanently remove or cryptographically/semantically make inaccessible the memory according to the existing storage abstraction.
* Ensure normal get/query/retrieval/context/replay APIs cannot return erased memories.
* Ensure erased IDs/keys cannot be restored.
* Ensure event replay cannot reconstruct erased data.
* Emit a safe audit/erasure event that does NOT contain the erased sensitive payload.
* Preserve auditability without preserving the erased personal data itself.
* Make the operation idempotent.
* Handle partial failures safely.
* Do not claim legal/GDPR compliance beyond the technical right-to-forget mechanism actually implemented.

Use terminology such as:

* erase
* erasure
* tombstone
* redaction

only where technically accurate.

Do NOT implement legal policy workflows or external compliance systems.

